---
layout: layouts/page.njk
title: "Gyeonggi-do Population-Decline Counties"
description: "The Gyeonggi-do counties designated as population-decline or watch-list areas, which qualify for the F-1-D visa's lower, non-capital income threshold."
permalink: "/regions/gyeonggi-do/population-decline-counties/"
---
{# Not paginated like regions/region.njk — there's only one region this data can ever affect
   (architecture.md §7: Gyeonggi-do is the only capital-tier region, so it's the only place a
   population-decline county can change the eligibility outcome). Built the same way as a region
   page otherwise: same .content-page/.region-header shell, same .city-list pattern already used
   for cities.json entries (region.njk) reused here for county entries — same shape (English/
   Korean name + a category badge), just a different data source. #}
<div class="content-page">
<header class="region-header">
  <h1>Gyeonggi-do population-decline counties</h1>
  <p class="region-header__intro">
    Gyeonggi-do is a capital-tier region for F-1-D visa purposes, so its income threshold is the
    country's highest — except in the counties below, which the government separately designates
    as population-decline or watch-list areas. Those counties qualify at the lower, non-capital
    threshold even though they sit administratively inside Gyeonggi-do. This is the hatched area
    on the <a href="/#map">home page map</a>.
  </p>
</header>

<section class="region-section">
  <h2>Qualifying counties</h2>
  <ul class="city-list">
    {% for county in populationDeclineAreas %}
    {% set countyPhoto = countyHeroPhotos[county.countyNameEn] %}
    {% set countyCredit = countyHeroCredits.photos[countyPhoto] %}
    <li class="city-list__item">
      {% if countyPhoto %}
      <img class="city-list__photo" src="/assets/img/hero/{{ countyPhoto }}" alt="{{ countyCredit.titleEn }}" loading="lazy">
      {% if countyCredit.titleEn %}
      <p class="city-list__photo-caption">
        <span class="city-list__photo-caption-en">{{ countyCredit.titleEn }}</span>
        {% if countyCredit.titleKo %}<span class="city-list__photo-caption-ko">{{ countyCredit.titleKo }}</span>{% endif %}
      </p>
      {% endif %}
      {% endif %}
      <h3>{{ county.countyNameEn }} <span class="city-list__ko">{{ county.countyNameKo }}</span></h3>
      <p>{{ county.metroEn }}</p>
      <p class="city-list__badge">{% if county.category == "decline" %}Population-decline-designated area{% else %}Population watch-list area{% endif %}</p>
    </li>
    {% endfor %}
  </ul>
  <p class="data-provenance">Photo source: © Korea Tourism Organization (한국관광공사).</p>
  <p class="data-provenance">
    Source: Ministry of the Interior and Safety (행정안전부) 인구감소지역 designation, sourced
    2026-08-18. See <a href="/visa-info/">visa income thresholds</a> for the full rules, and the
    <a href="/regions/gyeonggi-do/">Gyeonggi-do region page</a> for general living info.
  </p>
</section>
</div>
